#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064246 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064100 :question/id #uuid "804f45cd-2082-5521-b4db-a32169716626" :question/math-academy-id "e-492" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc6023d1-1461-50d1-b939-7e08f2878df4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050489 :topic/math-academy-id 478 :topic/title "Integrating Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1af2e84f-a21d-52e3-a64a-4cd4f75a12e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257011} {:answer/id #uuid "9c127a15-e250-5fec-ba10-64265f125da9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258153} {:answer/id #uuid "a52d209e-bc78-5754-8593-120bb1521e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258221} {:answer/id #uuid "ab28af47-d9d9-51e6-a7e7-784bf7544716" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258275} {:answer/id #uuid "b11f0972-d6c7-5f7c-b041-100cfd94fdbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a52d209e-bc78-5754-8593-120bb1521e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258221} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec602d5e-cc1e-5573-8422-898b9eb55e75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259444}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f405e14-26e8-524b-b2bf-2f3fef1fc543" :question/math-academy-id "q-12564" :question/problem "$\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+3)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043fa24a-45ec-5b10-bfa8-7e31faa50866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272422} {:answer/id #uuid "4dad317a-7e2c-5027-9a3a-188de187c660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273038} {:answer/id #uuid "657c9906-4184-54b2-a2ca-75931266448c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273256} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6fa9bf-7209-5009-8683-0533f03518a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274192} {:answer/id #uuid "ef13a328-66f5-517d-8b0a-ca4c0258e019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef13a328-66f5-517d-8b0a-ca4c0258e019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274503} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b869c77-052f-508f-90ff-9807f6d71398" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274873}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36f423a0-7a02-5e68-b537-f427610136e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-14437" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6729e761-a109-51c4-8606-18751a53f95b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248350} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf1abf3-9f83-5499-84e8-2cdbf9e21301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248682} {:answer/id #uuid "aeaf0778-2cce-5ff4-8bd6-a8910cbdb116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248985} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e5714-4c05-5edb-b661-6e6122f8d589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3b4c5a-2810-58be-abbd-d2691adfd127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249108} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7740ab9-c0ff-5f8c-91e3-87881adad76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249964}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8a77892-fbcb-5fb9-802a-ce425028c881" :question/math-academy-id "q-114297" :question/problem "$\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250230 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95bc501d-4124-5179-a51b-315ac85a1b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248757} {:answer/id #uuid "9f69fd84-e05c-5d24-ae8e-9d8f383459c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248843} {:answer/id #uuid "dea80f9c-54f5-5396-b7ef-3e0d29ed1c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249399} {:answer/id #uuid "fc7731aa-f29b-5e06-aa8d-a528db3cff78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{4}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249627} {:answer/id #uuid "ff931226-3ee2-5a37-af2b-7544f41260e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{8}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95bc501d-4124-5179-a51b-315ac85a1b36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248757} :answer-field/id #uuid "75347d01-2014-547c-a5ad-13e10a343907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249869}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b188b68-b90e-5d2a-a750-30bfecf83280" :question/math-academy-id "q-114299" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\int \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} {:answer/id #uuid "ab51dc5a-a926-51cd-8e7b-df0870f057c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248946} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cbad19-d246-5b98-8980-41bddf12f22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249448} {:answer/id #uuid "e99bc9d8-a545-56d1-baef-23123e5ae336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{6}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249486} {:answer/id #uuid "f8073886-20e6-5ba4-879b-63835b53eb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21296bbd-9655-58f7-83aa-dba5af0c8f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247716} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9a9941-4c05-5900-9e9e-c028b2cee8de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249858}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64685827-c31f-5450-80d9-3d65e9e828de" :question/math-academy-id "q-114309" :question/problem "$\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+4)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+4)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250234 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0847d4a6-8406-569f-8fd9-6ee28d2c43d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247496} {:answer/id #uuid "9604a7f9-7867-5499-9942-d113f7cabdb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248760} {:answer/id #uuid "b4bb6439-052e-5829-9382-493c51eccdba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249041} {:answer/id #uuid "f40de5b1-3fd0-5afd-8a8c-b0a694969250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249561} {:answer/id #uuid "f9394f54-b364-5841-85eb-57a59630de67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0847d4a6-8406-569f-8fd9-6ee28d2c43d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247496} :answer-field/id #uuid "5624c3ea-4def-51b8-a6da-e1cf8c816d71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249828}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a36b9441-9ddb-586c-961c-0956d2121b3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114311" :question/problem "$\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+3\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (2x+3)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(2x+3)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(2x+3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250235 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c09516b-ffde-5c4c-8dbe-564104924571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{15}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248513} {:answer/id #uuid "a581301a-72c3-5cfb-8ef1-56abefe481a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{25}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248900} {:answer/id #uuid "a5873c57-b416-5bd2-86d9-681f98615c39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248901} {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ae0e29-77f1-5100-a586-609d2c797e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{15}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b120bf14-8c51-5072-89f4-30873910c7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249011} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea192b1-985a-504b-a59a-fe45ed09d88a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249781}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d0e94f6-1e93-555f-a728-ca5181d50236" :question/math-academy-id "q-114312" :question/problem "$\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e07b070-117b-50c5-9563-364f2b472707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247691} {:answer/id #uuid "55dba241-a0ad-5dd2-a193-a8f4b6a32a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248201} {:answer/id #uuid "73e6af66-30b4-53c1-9d1f-0d00e757eaa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{cos}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248442} {:answer/id #uuid "80fe39bd-6730-5d90-8ec2-9b32e504d4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248563} {:answer/id #uuid "fc349b75-7a3e-573b-affc-74cf566b5683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55dba241-a0ad-5dd2-a193-a8f4b6a32a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248201} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0fb41b9-ef63-543e-b53e-dffe53d28fbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250000}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ea7a186f-be1a-52b9-b47f-3320d955e3e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-114314" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡x\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={csc}^{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ where $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{csc}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0532f827-efa9-5943-921e-cd8747195164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡5x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272435} {:answer/id #uuid "a34610b7-078b-5a23-bfdf-b83fba68fb35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273796} {:answer/id #uuid "aa05f3bb-4c79-5366-99b2-4194d18ca74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273855} {:answer/id #uuid "ad550bfa-33c2-5773-873f-42e48064e922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273882} {:answer/id #uuid "c15bdd0d-cf56-529b-ba9a-ea8d3c6be943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad550bfa-33c2-5773-873f-42e48064e922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273882} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eeb4dbf-b5b3-5475-acd4-8a11aa7e8123" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274768}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "633e79f5-4963-57db-9237-badf9fbf96a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-14449" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=5 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 5x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 5\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06faa5e0-4af8-5348-9efd-11165c5b749d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272448} {:answer/id #uuid "316a580c-b1ad-519a-9924-7acafc208775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272829} {:answer/id #uuid "515140df-a38b-5675-b2b8-0083349b8513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273080} {:answer/id #uuid "632167df-25c2-51dc-8e43-73f4595dd519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273239} {:answer/id #uuid "e8961a49-7238-5263-89a6-7dc02e214375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8961a49-7238-5263-89a6-7dc02e214375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274443} :answer-field/id #uuid "00d03065-2e89-51a1-b42e-23e110a6964b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274638}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efa8bb83-66d2-57ab-8d51-71c6b76f0e3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-14453" :question/problem "$\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))+C \\\\  & =6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c9bf20-8128-53fc-aa86-1964b815386d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339304} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb7e5b-2acb-5ebe-ad55-584b08e3b9c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} {:answer/id #uuid "534af3da-95e9-55b2-aba8-6f4b454b8ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339896} {:answer/id #uuid "90dc551e-639b-50fc-9023-134528ddbdd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340425} {:answer/id #uuid "c5917a7f-b9e8-5505-bca8-86a9c397ec2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eeb7e5b-2acb-5ebe-ad55-584b08e3b9c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339845} :answer-field/id #uuid "64dee0d1-0120-5112-8fc9-ab060cbba4c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341556}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6203036f-b82a-557b-b713-2351ced43cc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-74087" :question/problem "Calculate  $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)}{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x+8)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+8)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d4e53ff-430e-5b10-b738-cd8dd3d0256b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339385} {:answer/id #uuid "4b9151d3-7fde-540f-b82e-0580c7384593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{6}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339807} {:answer/id #uuid "989f6c04-735e-50e5-8fdd-bb014b8275b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340506} {:answer/id #uuid "add28c3c-0b54-53af-97fb-51c4b2116412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} {:answer/id #uuid "f90418c6-311c-5a49-b4cf-0366851ed196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{6}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "add28c3c-0b54-53af-97fb-51c4b2116412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340712} :answer-field/id #uuid "0614f8dc-7023-5386-a910-5a8612abf41b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341396}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b94b38f3-a670-562e-93ec-c45c6d3b0d77" :question/math-academy-id "q-74088" :question/problem "$\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (6x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(6x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e99b757-9d06-5cfc-8db6-a2492878332c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)}{10}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339262} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4fd180-d811-5662-8d7f-8cf39e6abded" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)}{10}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339651} {:answer/id #uuid "73d61482-1a92-5fde-a598-f549899e13ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f2d102-e8a3-564e-981d-58e57522a465" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340754} {:answer/id #uuid "da9ff3c8-cb06-5827-af7c-d34ff6bef005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73d61482-1a92-5fde-a598-f549899e13ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340154} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a2565c-7c88-5b3a-b2f9-3d057c775bea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341789}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31ac68e1-bc05-5634-b712-63c327f4e3c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-74090" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=10x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=10 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 10x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 10x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-10\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9775c1a1-be1f-5d4a-8b38-2b22b3877645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+5)}{3}+\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363005} {:answer/id #uuid "25af2b05-29e6-557b-85e3-77fd7abe9e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363006} {:answer/id #uuid "91cb4a25-ae24-57be-8930-89439bfcd808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363007} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b7d50e-bf4c-5d3c-8f65-093e0d804de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{9}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363008} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c244ca-ce7e-5f14-8b4e-fc2f90fec15c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cb4a25-ae24-57be-8930-89439bfcd808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363007} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5a6fdb-0204-5d6b-854a-5929492322cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d889fae-ff07-5704-acc9-b1fed02f79be" :question/math-academy-id "q-12565" :question/problem "Calculate  $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+5)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+5)}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b416a21d-f860-5ddd-9887-3909cbcfc268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367605} {:answer/id #uuid "84ff0b6d-4bc8-58b4-8c1f-7733a5d10ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367606} {:answer/id #uuid "8e61b06f-5796-5daf-a560-740f317dd6f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}+\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367607} {:answer/id #uuid "52c4db08-6d75-5662-ba65-98e14935cb32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367608} {:answer/id #uuid "665ef108-98da-5b42-b5b6-51f12caa5073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84ff0b6d-4bc8-58b4-8c1f-7733a5d10ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367606} :answer-field/id #uuid "7906d722-793f-554d-8af3-30e86eebaf11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367604}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c948087e-b394-5663-8b66-c2d6a56d25e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-14451" :question/problem "$\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing a Trigonometric Expression"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064259 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064104 :question/id #uuid "fe999c48-1afd-5949-b4f9-533c09511d95" :question/math-academy-id "e-5295" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=3x^2+1$ where the tangent line has a slope of $-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3x^2+1.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to $f'(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}+1) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2x+0 \\\\  & =6x+0 \\\\  & =6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set $f'(x) = -1$ and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-1 \\\\ 6x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-1$ at the point where $x=-\\dfrac 1 6.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a74f63-a4eb-5894-b4a4-eb4fd297a3f3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac7a76ac-6a4f-5fcf-bae5-d1c77080f767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063074} {:answer/id #uuid "0416d290-23bb-5e98-b9c4-91cbf661f485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063075} {:answer/id #uuid "09675fc0-f33d-5fc0-89f0-d749e9d1887e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063076} {:answer/id #uuid "2197b5a0-b9e9-5025-8543-c899cd7620da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063077} {:answer/id #uuid "5e0ebb24-4f4a-50af-adb4-bc9ba0c0a760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063078}] :answer-field/id #uuid "38c2e43f-175e-5efa-a0f9-922bc22223b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063073}] :question/id #uuid "f161b0b1-fa28-5b06-904e-0f125cbd11ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-48692" :question/problem "Find the positive $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y = x^{3} - 2x^{2} - 5x$ where the tangent has a slope of $27$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4875dd9-2f2f-50e9-9229-899321a98be0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063086} {:answer/id #uuid "e5edbde9-ed52-5d76-9538-892cadde3139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063087} {:answer/id #uuid "0d08936b-484d-5b37-95c7-3f9f9b99e9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063088} {:answer/id #uuid "5adc5944-8a2c-55c2-8a3d-a236e1831693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063089} {:answer/id #uuid "6c8a971d-a0fa-5e2e-aded-45861f4c5153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063090}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3df1a573-1d68-53fb-b72c-d4e4143dea91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063085}] :question/id #uuid "1f5f60f6-00c8-5638-895e-53f7fe6066ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-48816" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y = x^{3} + 3x^{2} + 6x - 3$ whose tangent has a slope of $3$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24eb5b98-ebae-51b3-a13b-4e26123c7b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24eb5b98-ebae-51b3-a13b-4e26123c7b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234602} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d9dea25-7475-5274-b13f-c513541575ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235093}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffc5990e-58cd-5fb4-8d5d-6325acc47d62" :question/math-academy-id "q-128236" :question/problem "Find the value of $k$ such that the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at the point where $x=0$ is equal to $0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $k\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Previously, we found that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+4x+k+8}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{-{0}^{2}+4\\cdot 0+k+8}{{({0}^{2}+4\\cdot 0+k)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{k+8}{{k}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve when $x=0$ equals $\\frac{k+8}{{k}^{2}}.$\n\nFinally, using the fact that  the slope must be equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k+8}{{k}^{2}} & =0 \\\\ k+8 & =0 \\\\ k & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=-8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15cb32d6-e3c9-5af9-adf2-a692df98b68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235949} {:answer/id #uuid "6c9a09c6-91ab-59c4-9d1f-73846c3d3762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236500} {:answer/id #uuid "9f6f5713-2692-5054-9c21-9ee31ea6a063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236811} {:answer/id #uuid "a2bad11c-69be-51cb-88d1-38ec8e11cf4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236837} {:answer/id #uuid "fac87a4a-b849-5cd5-9db2-357a32264549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fac87a4a-b849-5cd5-9db2-357a32264549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237403} :answer-field/id #uuid "69b53a83-54bf-552e-959d-837340db83d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237576}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b74e076-1211-5eb5-9bb6-77fa9cea478c" :question/math-academy-id "q-102236" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{2}-3x+10$ whose tangent has a slope of $-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-3x+10.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-3x+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =2x-3\\cdot 1+0 \\\\  & =2x-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=-1$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =-1 \\\\ 2x & =-1+3 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-1$ at the point where $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1188c1c5-041f-544a-b56f-637e6b3210a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1188c1c5-041f-544a-b56f-637e6b3210a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315225} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dfed7b7-234b-56dc-92da-55f47773a03f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316870}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba8bd60a-e86a-5439-823a-fbaac32bf4b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-343735" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3$ whose tangent has a slope of $1.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+4x-3.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+4x-3) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =2(2x)+4(1) \\\\  & =4x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=1$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4 & =1 \\\\ 4x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $1$ at the point where $x=-\\frac{3}{4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a02d079-b422-5894-aa35-d332e8ddf027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a02d079-b422-5894-aa35-d332e8ddf027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315357} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa3617b-42b1-5250-ba3e-34a78514594c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316606}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da3c67ed-99d8-57ba-b0f5-8fc958679a71" :question/math-academy-id "q-343737" :question/problem "Find the **positive** $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6$ whose tangent has a slope of $22.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x+14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=22$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+2x+14 & =22 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the positive $x$-coordinate of the points whose tangent has a slope of $6,$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eaebcbd-9756-50eb-bd1d-5df67107c5f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327200} {:answer/id #uuid "76095c4e-fe50-5e62-a537-b4a30720bfe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327946} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0124b8-1270-54e6-85c6-b6c4821e0345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328265} {:answer/id #uuid "a11fde28-0164-5479-b55c-449aff8e5bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\,1." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328332} {:answer/id #uuid "f75dcddb-213f-536c-96ae-50a77358eeb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f75dcddb-213f-536c-96ae-50a77358eeb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329105} :answer-field/id #uuid "587f04fc-1b5a-59da-ba85-fcbbd60d19f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329343}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac72967c-0395-50e5-812a-2bfe9c19348f" :question/math-academy-id "q-48817" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinates of the points on the curve $y=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1$ whose tangent has a slope of $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+20\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+6\\cdot 2x+20\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2}+12x+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=2$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+12x+20 & =2 \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6({x}^{2}-2x-3) & =0 \\\\ -6(x+1)(x-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $2$ at the points where $x=-1,3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b7e5c24-b468-5f5c-883f-c5b1e1e084fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327595} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ec0c79-d6b9-5f7b-960d-15e625a262d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328369} {:answer/id #uuid "c0cfbdb6-072d-56a8-8195-bb416d7fab9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328617} {:answer/id #uuid "d48c566d-f478-5e1b-9ffe-f431bd6b60af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328794} {:answer/id #uuid "f13fa932-2f22-5b2e-827d-657bb2e42b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0cfbdb6-072d-56a8-8195-bb416d7fab9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328617} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2caaacf-1c65-5c7a-a909-643a5e83d927" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329460}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cec8f053-a5c3-52d0-be5b-db70ebab81b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-48970" :question/problem "Find the positive $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4$ whose tangent has a slope of $6.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4) \\\\  & =8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-3\\cdot 2x-12\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =24{x}^{2}-6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=6$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24{x}^{2}-6x-12 & =6 \\\\ 24{x}^{2}-6x-18 & =0 \\\\ 6(4{x}^{2}-x-3) & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)(4x+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $6$ at the point where $x=1$ and $x=-\\frac{3}{4}.$ Since $x>0$, our answer is $x=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510720 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4fa0cb2-db6a-5c95-a80a-4cdb79568c03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4fa0cb2-db6a-5c95-a80a-4cdb79568c03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510722} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc755ef9-cb44-5175-b229-7f7ea951429f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510721}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fd03b4b-26b0-57a3-90b6-cf64c012470d" :question/problem "Find the **positive** $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=- x^{3} + 42 x - 2$ whose tangent has a slope of $-6.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=- x^{3} + 42 x - 2.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to $f^{\\prime}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime}(x) &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- x^{3} + 42 x - 2\\right) \\\\\n&= (-1)\\cdot 3\\cdot x^{2} + (42)\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 42 - 3 x^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set $f^{\\prime}(x)=-6$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n42 - 3 x^{2} &= -6 \\\\\n48 - 3 x^{2} &= 0 \\\\\n- 3 \\left(x - 4\\right) \\left(x + 4\\right) &= 0 \\\\\nx &= -4,\\,4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x>0$, the required coordinate is $x=4.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Curve With a Certain Slope"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064274 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064117 :question/id #uuid "aaeb0407-771b-5dbc-8a50-e7bc0e3477c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-6209" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "398c3cee-657c-5b95-8a1e-1aa70b615cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330468} {:answer/id #uuid "4b6624a0-3597-520a-b136-40dc699a2c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330632} {:answer/id #uuid "829fe91a-9a59-5b71-9364-170b07c5eb54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331102} {:answer/id #uuid "b6aee3a4-6d54-578c-8449-e0741c41a98f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331563} {:answer/id #uuid "cea8bab6-1bfc-5d6a-a36b-eda9ee31a503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "829fe91a-9a59-5b71-9364-170b07c5eb54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a32b33d9-9824-5fca-9f78-08bd81319767" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332487}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d08b82b1-573b-56aa-9196-6973e5625acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-49664" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & ⇒ & v=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)]+[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0]+[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e635c6-8362-502a-8dac-9f4c126f56b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330682} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2cbd9a-7afc-5459-b6df-7ca6506a12c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330765} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4d14d4-eed1-5e2e-b017-564cb00a0993" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9e}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331378} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8743c8-cccb-54cd-b8ac-95180b80ba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331757} {:answer/id #uuid "cd91e0dd-3fb4-57cb-8cdd-dff11939eaf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd91e0dd-3fb4-57cb-8cdd-dff11939eaf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331772} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dfe59be-f622-58ca-a168-a466d2025ba6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332341}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49de41a8-b520-5e5d-99f3-b4a02784a3b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-49684" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}2x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{3x} & ⇒ & v=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}2x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{2}{3}x{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3}-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}{e}^{3x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2}{3}x{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3}-{\\frac{2}{9}{e}^{3x}|}_{0}^{1/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3(1/3)}-0\\cdot {e}^{3\\cdot 0}]-\\frac{2}{9}[{e}^{3(1/3)}-{e}^{3\\cdot 0}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{e}{3}-0]-\\frac{2}{9}[e-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{2e}{9}-\\frac{2e}{9}+\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771a4680-23b4-5532-bdca-e5e5e51c2e8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248472} {:answer/id #uuid "788019d8-4726-57ee-8d3c-f8c472f663ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248481} {:answer/id #uuid "938dda6d-62d5-5932-8236-a8efaf7f79ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248736} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} {:answer/id #uuid "ac64494d-e051-58cd-912e-6906743c182e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa8bee3f-8a28-593e-a9b3-8c87ee384d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248941} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc9c08d-e5e1-5b3f-9652-c2d450c9f225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249886}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ecbdeecb-1f0c-572b-8510-8e18414c1281" :question/math-academy-id "q-114320" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-2x} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-2x}}{2})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x{e}^{-2x}}{2}{|}_{-1}^{0}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-2x}{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0{e}^{-2(0)}-(-1){e}^{-2(-1)}]-\\frac{3}{4}[{e}^{-2(0)}-{e}^{-2(-1)}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0+{e}^{2}]-\\frac{3}{4}[1-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e72326f-b37b-556e-9771-d69f461e0b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248129} {:answer/id #uuid "5979c57e-1a61-504f-9748-c153fbd57b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248234} {:answer/id #uuid "82511b39-0f0e-5f20-82f8-c82314f7aca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248578} {:answer/id #uuid "941618c9-aa44-56dd-b179-4d773a5937a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248740} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f13165-476e-58f7-beb6-a83b3ddfdb39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5979c57e-1a61-504f-9748-c153fbd57b43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248234} :answer-field/id #uuid "8956bd65-6e03-5145-875e-cd65f5f6055b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249909}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b71aa220-d93a-5e59-b207-8dade0373ae4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114322" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))-\\int (-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)}{4}|}_{0}^{\\pi }+{\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi )}{4}+\\frac{0\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot 0)}{4}] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{16}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0)+\\frac{1}{16}(0-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d83e583-d218-50f4-abb7-474c6d01c304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247546} {:answer/id #uuid "3d047995-440b-51a6-837d-6a9c0a9dea33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247961} {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7776ae-27e1-5fb2-91d8-1d3d11b460fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248680} {:answer/id #uuid "aea67226-a698-5829-a7e0-c9089694e776" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4217347b-9b32-5330-8c51-bcd370f084c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248013} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff430e6-479c-5fff-ae3c-19a79a5cfe3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249818}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37affd24-3b4f-536c-8927-723157249685" :question/math-academy-id "q-114328" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{9}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d8920c-9eae-5d0e-8971-ca7e7b55533e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2e-3}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248477} {:answer/id #uuid "7b577e2d-1a9b-598e-a5bb-8e6d22918919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{e+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248506} {:answer/id #uuid "82f9